.TH RECONFORGE 1 "August 2026" "ReconForge v0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reconforge \- Offline reconnaissance analyzer and planning tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reconforge
[\fITARGET\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B reconforge
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ReconForge is an offline log analyzer designed for authorized penetration testing environments. It imports raw outputs from Nmap, Gobuster, and other security tools, normalizing and correlating them. Additionally, it offers an interactive planning mode capable of generating structured execution plans based on provided IPs and URLs without executing external network calls directly.
.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
Running \fBreconforge\fR without arguments launches the interactive mode, prompting for Mode, Target Type, and Port Configuration.
.SH TARGET MODES
.B reconforge 10.48.159.132
.br
.B reconforge -u http://10.48.159.132:5000
.br
.B reconforge --url https://example.com
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --mode standard
Plans default enumeration using all applicable installed tools.
.TP
.B --mode low-impact
WAF-Aware Low-Impact Recon. Configures the execution plan constraints to respect rate-limits, Retry-After headers, and avoid duplicate/evasive requests.
.TP
.B --version
Displays the installed ReconForge version (v0.2.0).
.TP
.B --test
Runs the built-in testing workflow.
.SH OFFLINE ANALYSIS
.B reconforge import <dir>
.br
Imports an entire directory of scan results and stores them in a session.
.br
.B reconforge analyze <file>
.br
Analyzes a single file and outputs the parsed intelligence.
.SH SESSIONS AND REPORTS
.B reconforge sessions
.br
Lists historical sessions.
.br
.B reconforge show current
.br
Displays summary of the latest session.
.br
.B reconforge report current --format html
.br
Generates a report for the latest session (supported formats: terminal, json, html).
.br
.B reconforge waf current
.br
Outputs the WAF and CDN analysis for the latest session.
.SH TOOL REGISTRY
.B reconforge tools
.br
Checks the availability of registered tools (e.g., Nmap, Gobuster) via the internal Tool Registry adapters.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
reconforge
reconforge 10.48.159.132 --mode low-impact
reconforge analyze tests/fixtures/sample.xml
reconforge import tests/fixtures/
reconforge report current --format terminal
reconforge waf current
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error.
